#X text 900 1320 §6.5 dispatch SPINE (ALLOW): [dispatch_op <pattern> <op>( -> unpack -> select the resolved HANDLER first (each handler body its own named unit - the FLOW-DESIGN spine) then the op-switch WITHIN it: tree get/put - capability request/revoke/configure/delegate - handlers register/unregister - validate echo / dispatch (reentry). An op outside the resolved handler's ladder -> 501 unsupported_operation \; an unauthored pattern (runtime-registered body) -> 501 not_implemented.;
#X obj 1180 1440 symbol;
#X obj 1180 1480 sel no_author no_capability;
#X text 1180 1520 §5.2a auth/authz split - a decode-time no_author is auth-class -> 401 (obj 38) / no_capability is authz-class -> 403 (obj 59) / every other authz_err reason -> 400 (obj 29). [symbol] coerces the [route] bare-selector (A-PD-007) before [sel].;
#X msg 900 1370 cap_request_serve;
#X msg 500 1145 op_supported \$1;
#X obj 500 1200 sel 0 1;
